<Routines>
<Routine Name="Home" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung is used to lock in the setup varibles for the Active home

(HomeMode)  0 = Passive, 1 = Active, 2 = Absolute

(Position) = Type the desired absolute position, in position units, for the axis after the specified homing sequence has been completed.  In most cases, this position will be set to zero, although any value within the software travel limits can be used.  After the homing sequence is complete, the axis is left in this position.
 
(Offset) = Type the desired offset (if any) in position units the axis is to move, upon completion of the homing sequence, to reach the home position.  In most cases, this value will be zero.

Sequence = Select the event that will cause the Home Position to be set: Immediate (0), Switch (1), Marker (2), Switch-Marker (3) 

HomeDirection = The homing direction mode for your axis.Value: 0 = Forward Uni-directional, 1 = Forward Bi-directional, 2 = Reverse Uni-directional, 3 = Reverse Bi-directional

Speed = Type the speed of the jog profile used in the first leg of an active homing sequence.  The homing speed specified should be less than the maximum speed and greater than zero.
 
Return Speed = The speed of the jog profile used in the return leg(s) of an active homing sequence.  The home return speed specified should be less than the maximum speed and greater than zero.
 
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Home_Ladder.Basic_Index.Index,10)MOV(1,Home_Ladder.Active_Home_Set.Mode)MOV(0,Home_Ladder.Active_Home_Set.Position)MOV(0,Home_Ladder.Active_Home_Set.Offset)MOV(2,Home_Ladder.Active_Home_Set.Sequence)MOV(1,Home_Ladder.Active_Home_Set.Direction)MOV(1,Home_Ladder.Active_Home_Set.Speed)MOV(0.1,Home_Ladder.Active_Home_Set.Return_Speed)MOV(15,Home_Ladder.Basic_Index.Index);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Home_Ladder.Basic_Index.Index,15)[XIC(Servo_Drive.DriveEnableStatus) MSF(Servo_Drive,Home_Ladder.MSF[0]) ,XIO(Servo_Drive.DriveEnableStatus) ]MOV(20,Home_Ladder.Basic_Index.Index);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[(HomeMode)
The homing mode for your axis.

0 = Passive:
  In this mode, homing redefines the absolute position of the axis on the occurrence of a home switch or encoder marker event.  Passive homing is most commonly used to calibrate uncontrolled axes, although it can also be used with controlled axes to create a custom homing sequence.  Passive homing, for a given home sequence, works similar to the corresponding active homing sequence, except that no motion is commanded; the controller just waits for the switch and marker events to occur.

1 = Active:
  In this mode, the desired homing sequence is selected by specifying whether a home limit switch and/or the encoder marker is used for this axis.  Active homing sequences always use the trapezoidal velocity profile.

2 = Absolute:
  (AXIS_SERVO_DRIVE, and AXIS_SERVO when associated with to a 1756-HYD02 module only)  In this mode, the absolute homing process establishes the true absolute position of the axis by applying the configured Home Position to the reported position of the absolute feedback device.  The only valid Home Sequence for an absolute Homing Mode is immediate.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Home_Ladder.Basic_Index.Index,20)MOV(0,Home_Ladder.Read_Back_Active_Home_Values.Mode)SSV(AXIS,Servo_Drive,HomeMode,Home_Ladder.Active_Home_Set.Mode)MOV(30,Home_Ladder.Basic_Index.Index);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[(HomeMode)
The homing mode for your axis.

0 = Passive:
  In this mode, homing redefines the absolute position of the axis on the occurrence of a home switch or encoder marker event.  Passive homing is most commonly used to calibrate uncontrolled axes, although it can also be used with controlled axes to create a custom homing sequence.  Passive homing, for a given home sequence, works similar to the corresponding active homing sequence, except that no motion is commanded; the controller just waits for the switch and marker events to occur.

1 = Active:
  In this mode, the desired homing sequence is selected by specifying whether a home limit switch and/or the encoder marker is used for this axis.  Active homing sequences always use the trapezoidal velocity profile.

2 = Absolute:
  (AXIS_SERVO_DRIVE, and AXIS_SERVO when associated with to a 1756-HYD02 module only)  In this mode, the absolute homing process establishes the true absolute position of the axis by applying the configured Home Position to the reported position of the absolute feedback device.  The only valid Home Sequence for an absolute Homing Mode is immediate.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Home_Ladder.Basic_Index.Index,30)XIO(Servo_Drive.ConfigUpdateInProcess)GSV(AXIS,Servo_Drive,HomeMode,Home_Ladder.Read_Back_Active_Home_Values.Mode)EQU(Home_Ladder.Active_Home_Set.Mode,Home_Ladder.Read_Back_Active_Home_Values.Mode)MOV(40,Home_Ladder.Basic_Index.Index);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Type the desired absolute position, in position units, for the axis after the specified homing sequence has been completed.  In most cases, this position will be set to zero, although any value within the software travel limits can be used.  After the homing sequence is complete, the axis is left in this position.
 
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Home_Ladder.Basic_Index.Index,40)MOV(0,Home_Ladder.Read_Back_Active_Home_Values.Position)SSV(AXIS,Servo_Drive,HomePosition,Home_Ladder.Active_Home_Set.Position)MOV(50,Home_Ladder.Basic_Index.Index);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
