<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[HomeDirection
The homing direction mode for your axis.Value:
 
0 = Forward Uni-directional
The axis jogs in the positive axial direction until a homing event (switch or marker) is encountered, then continues in the same direction until axis motion stops (after decelerating or moving the Offset distance).

1 = Forward Bi-directional
The axis jogs in the positive axial direction until a homing event (switch or marker) is encountered, then reverses direction until motion stops (after decelerating or moving the Offset distance).

2 = Reverse Uni-directional
The axis jogs in the negative axial direction until a homing event (switch or marker) is encountered, then continues in the same direction until axis motion stops (after decelerating or moving the Offset distance).

3 = Reverse Bi-directional
The axis jogs in the negative axial direction until a homing event (switch or marker) is encountered, then reverses direction until motion stops (after decelerating or moving the Offset distance).
 
]]>
</Comment>
